From 9bfd13fe3c67a7cd88fe76f90c1059054cc72642 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sak-114514 <Sak-114514@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:58:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Keep TP3 production reversible while measuring native MTP
 capacity

The AC922 coding API now has an isolated TP3 service path that preserves its
existing key and middleware. Native MTP uses a separate checkpoint config, so
its one BF16 attention layer and MLP need the same in-memory TP3 expansion as
the target. The MTP path remains opt-in for a bounded trial while DFlash2
continues to serve production.

Constraint: Three 16GB V100s, local Qwen3.8-27B AWQ and MTP checkpoints, no reboot
Rejected: Replace production with MTP after two requests | concurrent stability and output quality are unverified
Confidence: medium
Scope-risk: moderate
Reversibility: clean
Directive: Do not enable the MTP trial as production without capacity, quality, and concurrent-request gates
Tested: Ruff check/format; shell syntax; TP3 target/draft config smoke; seven real BF16 MTP tensor transforms; 1k and 64k streamed requests with 128 output tokens and no OOM
Not-tested: 200k MTP request, 30-minute stability, multi-client concurrency, full-project CI, reboot
